      "writtenOn": "2018-11-16T20:53:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand you\u0027re just doing the same thing as for the specifier, but I don\u0027t think this is right. First, I think it may definitely make sense in the case of a VPN which may have multiple transports. Then, while I understand that this has to come from some concrete network provider and that they do all have some technology, I\u0027m not sure how fundamentally intrictated that is ; at least I think it\u0027s disjoint enough that it should be okay to set the meta capabilities before the the transport when building a NetworkCapabilites object that describes a specific network.\n\nI\u0027d vote to simply remove this part and the comment and the throw. (and probably in the future also remove the same test for the network specifier)",
